   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 has no automatic sales stop for models above 5%, which is the key weakening and lets the Hearth 10 (6.2%) remain on sale during corrective action; customers do receive numeric rates while public disclosure is barred. S3 gives a 72-month retrofit window, which favours Northwind's low 38% shut-off coverage, and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months, which favours Halcyon's higher suppression cost. S5 mandates recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which constrains Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9."
 },
